<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Untash-Napirisha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Untash-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napirisha">Napirisha</a> was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> in the fourteenth century BCE. He built the religious complex of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chogha-zanbil">Chogha Zanbil</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>, centred on a great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziggurat">ziggurat</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> date its construction to around 1340 BCE, notes that it is now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>, and treats it as evidence of the state's capacity to mobilise resources.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/untash-napirisha.jpg" alt="Untash-Napirisha" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fabienkhan · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Axe_Sb_3973.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
